cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Vector Abliteration Units in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Vector Abliteration Units (VAU): a standard for units that change what a model does from inside"
abstract: >-
  A unit standard and host library for operations on a model's activations and weights:
  each unit is one file that declares its parameters and the kind of place in a model it
  acts on, and a host loads, checks and runs units. Part of the Vector Lab family of
  research instruments.
type: software
authors:
